title: FastUnlock - Program Launched From Removable Media as WsiAccount
id: 8f1c4a52-6f4d-4b1e-9d0a-2c7b5e93af14
status: experimental
description: Detects the FastUnlock Windows 11 lock-screen bypass, where a physically present attacker uses Narrator to reach SystemSettings and Explorer, mounts a USB drive and runs a binary as the ephemeral non-administrative WsiAccount without signing in. WsiAccount executing an image from a non-system drive letter is the observable residue of that flow.
references:
  - https://thehackernews.com/2026/11/new-unpatched-windows-0-day-fastunlock.html
  - https://www.threatlocker.com/blog/proof-of-concept-for-fastunlock-windows-lock-screen-bypass-from-nightmare-eclipse
  - https://github.com/MSNightmare/FastUnlock
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/11/21
tags:
  - attack.t1200
logsource:
  product: windows
  category: process_creation
detection:
  selection_user:
    User|endswith: '\WsiAccount'
  selection_external_media:
    Image|re: '^[d-zD-Z]:\\'
  filter_integrity:
    IntegrityLevel: 'System'
  condition: selection_user and selection_external_media and not filter_integrity
falsepositives:
  - Legitimate provisioning or imaging runs that launch signed vendor tools from a removable drive under the WsiAccount context
  - Backup and recovery software executing from external media while running as WsiAccount
level: medium
